 to resources on the computer on which the group is created. Local groups can have any user accounts that are local to the computer as members, as well as users, groups, and computers from a domain to which the computer belongs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="76022">local group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467602">स्थानिक समूह</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12547_155493_468107"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technical document in the Microsoft Knowledge Base accessible through Microsoft.com.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="155493">KB article</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="468107">KB लेख</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12548_139813_467993"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user dictionary that contains a list of words not in the application dictionary that an author wants the spelling checker to accept as correct.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="139813">custom dictionary</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467993">सानुकूल शब्दकोश</term><termNote type="geographicalU