 id="338601">Home Screen</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1959201">होम स्क्रीन</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13772_52156_467446"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to a type of access to data in a database that is shared over a network. When you open a database in exclusive mode, you prevent others from opening the database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="52156">exclusive</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467446">एकाधिकार</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13776_5615_467080"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A supplemental program that can extend the capabilities of an application program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="5615">add-in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467080">ऍड-इन</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13787_397179_1959239"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of recipients that are created to expedite the mass emailing of messages and other information. Unlike a mail-enabled universal distribution group, a mail-enabled USG can also be used to assign permissions. When email is sent to a mail-enabled USG, all members of that group receive a copy of the message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397179">mail-enabled universal security group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1959239">मेल सक्षम वैश्विक सुरक्षा समूह</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13788_213533_1962904"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To tap twice quickly on a screen or touchpad.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="213533">double-tap</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1962904">डबल टॅप करा</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1379_120227_467862"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The suite of networking protocols arranged in four layers, which are called the link layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer, and that includes IP in the internet layer and TCP in the transport layer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120227">TCP/IP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467862">TCP/IP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1379_120227_467863"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The suite of networking protocols arranged in four layers, which are called the link layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer, and that includes IP in the internet layer and TCP in the transport layer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120227">TCP/IP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467863">ट्रान्समिशन कंट्रोल प्रोटोकॉल/इंटरनेट प्रोटोकॉल</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1379_120228_467862"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The suite of networking protocols arranged in four layers, which are called the link layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer, and that includes IP in the internet layer and TCP in the transport layer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120228">Transmission Control Protocol/Internet Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467862">TCP/IP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNot