ble field.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="231975">PivotTable subtotal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1879535">PivotTable पोटबेरीज</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15317_126865_467899"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Easy to learn and easy to use.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="126865">user-friendly</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467899">प्रयोक्त्यासाठी सोपे</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15319_52477_2998313"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The operation in which a number is raised to a given power, as in 23. In computer programs and programming languages, exponentiation is often shown by a caret (^), as in 2^3.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="52477">exponentiation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2998313">घातांकीय</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15327_219610_1424967"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The control panel for Office (including the Tools Options dialog).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="219610">Resources</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1424967">संसाधने</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15332_397204_1959254"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Records management technology in Exchange 2007 that helps organizations to reduce the risks that are associated with email and other communications. MRM makes it easier to keep messages that are needed to comply with company policy, government regulations, or legal needs, and to remove content that has no legal or business value.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397204">messaging records management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1959254">संदेश रेकॉर्ड व्‍यवस्‍थापन</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15332_397204_1959269"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Records management technology in Exchange 2007 that helps organizations to reduce the risks that are associated with email and other communications. MRM makes it easier to keep messages that are needed to comply with company policy, government regulations, or legal needs, and to remove content that has no legal or business value.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397204">messaging records management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1959269">MRM</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15332_397205_1959254"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Records management technology in Exchange 2007 that helps organizations to reduce the risks that are associated with email and other communications. MRM makes it easier to keep messages that are needed to comply with company policy, government regulations, or legal needs, and to remove content that has no legal or business value.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397205">MRM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1959254">संदेश रेकॉर्ड व्‍यवस्‍थापन</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15332_397205_1959269"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Records management technology in Exchange 2007 that helps organizations to reduce the risks that are associated with email and other communications. MRM makes it easier to keep messages that are needed to comply with company policy, government regulations, or legal needs, and to remove content that has no legal or business value.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397205">MRM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1959269">MRM</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15335_104365_467779"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To copy files from a backup storage device to their normal location, especially if the files are being copied to replace files that were accidentally lost or deleted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="104365">restore</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467779">पुनर्स्थापित करा</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1534_94749_467746"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A key on IBM PC and compatible keyboards that normally causes the computer to send a character-based “picture” of the screen contents to the printer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="94749">PRINT SCREEN key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="467746">PRINT SCREEN कळ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Femi