 only those in a specific department, region, or any segment that their organization defines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902145">administrative unit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902497">प्रशासनिक युनिट</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51589_2910377_2902497"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A conceptual container that allows a company administrator to restrict the users and groups that an admin can manage to only those in a specific department, region, or any segment that their organization defines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2910377">AU</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902497">प्रशासनिक युनिट</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51593_2902151_2902502"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An isolated group within an organizational structure that has little to no interaction with other groups, often leading to a lack of collaboration and other negative outcomes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902151">silo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902502">सिलो</term><term