Selected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6314_138412_1879409"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An animation enhancement that lets you apply effects to a chart by series, category, or element in a series or category.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="138412">chart effect option</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1879409">रेखाचित्र प्रभाव पर्याय</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6316_155655_1207787"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">For files, information that indicates whether a file is read-only, hidden, ready for archiving (backing up), compressed, or encrypted, and whether the file contents should be indexed for fast file searching.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="155655">attribute</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1207787">स्वाभाविकता</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6316_155655_1268861"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">For files, information that indicates whether a file is read-only, hidden, ready for archiving (backing up), compressed, or encrypted, and whether the file contents should be indexed for fast file searching.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="155655">attribute</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1268861">गुणधर्म</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6317_262429_468454"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A security method used by wireless networks. WPA encrypts the information that is sent between computers on a wireless network and authenticates users to help ensure that only authorized people can access the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262429">Wi-Fi Protected Access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="468454">Wi-Fi संरक्षित ऍक्सेस</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6317_262429_468455"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A security method used by wireless networks. WPA encrypts the information that is sent between computers on a wireless network and authenticates users to help ensure that only authorized people can access the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262429">Wi-Fi Protected Access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="468455">WPA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6317_262430_468454"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A security method used by wireless networks. WPA encrypts the information that is sent between computers on a wireless network and authenticates users to help ensure that only authorized people can access the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262430">WPA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="468454">Wi-Fi संरक्षित ऍक्सेस</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6317_262430_468455"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A security method used by wireless networks. WPA encrypts the information that is sent between computers on a wireless network and authenticates users to help ensure that only authorized people can access the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262430">WPA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="468455">WPA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6319_343640_468936"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of managing business and/or social contacts in order to follow up, track conversations, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="343640">contact management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="468936">संपर्क व्यवस्थापन</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6333_184278_2485914"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A BIOS developed to enable system-related information, such as information about hardware, to be gathered from computers on a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184278">SMBIOS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2485914">SMBIOS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6333_184279_2485914"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A BIOS developed to enable system-related information, such as information about hardware, to be gathered from computers on a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184279">system management BIOS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2485914">SMBIOS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6349_345311_1207788"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of arranging data based on the order of specified information. For example, records sorted by class would list all records within a class before moving to records in the next class.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="345311">sorting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1207788">क्रमवारी लावणे</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6350_276560_468572"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The utility in Windows Vista that presents a view of all PCs, devices, and printers on the network, and is significantly faster and more reliable than My Network Places in Windows XP.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="276560">Network Explorer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="468572">नेटवर्क एक्सप्लोरर</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6352_152788_2855804"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method by which a client receives a stream, during which he/she cannot control the stream.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="152788">broadcast</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">No