BA objects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="68675">interface definition language</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1795454">IDL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="699_731998_1795454"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In object-oriented programming, a language that lets a program or object written in one language communicate with another program written in an unknown language. An IDL is used to define interfaces between client and server programs. For example, an IDL can provide interfaces to remote CORBA objects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="731998">IDL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1795454">IDL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7002_157648_468123"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A time limit that is applied to the life of an account, so that it can be used only for a predetermined period of time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="157648">account expiration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="mr"><ntig><termGrp><term id="468123">खाते कालावधी समाप्ती</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">I